ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models
Project Development
1. Development Overview
The development of ComicCraft converts the requirements and design into a working AI-powered comic creation application. The implementation is divided into frontend development, backend development, database development, Gemini AI integration, comic editing, export, and testing.
The overall development flow is:
Project Setup
      ↓
Frontend Development
      ↓
Backend Development
      ↓
Database Integration
      ↓
Gemini Integration
      ↓
Comic Generation
      ↓
Comic Editor
      ↓
Preview & Export
      ↓
Testing
      ↓
Deployment
________________________________________
2. Development Environment
Frontend
A suitable frontend stack is:
•	React / Next.js
•	TypeScript
•	HTML5
•	CSS / Tailwind CSS
The frontend provides the user interface for creating and editing comics.
Backend
A suitable backend stack is:
•	Node.js
•	Express.js
•	TypeScript
The backend handles authentication, database operations, AI requests, file management, and export.
Database
•	PostgreSQL or MongoDB
The database stores users, projects, characters, pages, panels, and dialogue.
AI
•	Gemini models through the appropriate Google AI API/SDK.
Development Tools
•	VS Code
•	Git
•	GitHub
•	Postman
•	Figma
