11. Story Generation Development
The backend constructs a prompt using the user's project information.
Conceptually:
Generate a comic story based on:

Title: ...
Genre: ...
Story idea: ...
Target audience: ...
Number of pages: ...
Tone: ...

Return structured comic information containing:
- story summary
- characters
- scenes
- panels
- dialogue
- narration
- visual prompts
The AI response is then validated and stored.
________________________________________
12. Structured AI Response
The application should use structured data rather than relying on arbitrary AI-generated text.
Example:
{
  "title": "The Last Robot",
  "summary": "A robot searches for signs of life...",
  "characters": [
    {
      "name": "Rex",
      "role": "Protagonist",
      "personality": "Curious and brave"
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "panelNumber": 1,
      "scene": "An abandoned city",
      "narration": "The city had been silent for years.",
      "dialogue": [
        {
          "character": "Rex",
          "text": "Is anyone still here?"
        }
      ],
      "visualPrompt": "A futuristic abandoned city..."
    }
  ]
}
This response can be mapped directly into the database.
