14. Scene and Panel Generation
The generated story is divided into pages and panels.
Example:
Page 1
 ├── Panel 1 – Establishing scene
 ├── Panel 2 – Character introduction
 └── Panel 3 – Conflict

Page 2
 ├── Panel 4 – Character discovers problem
 ├── Panel 5 – Action
 └── Panel 6 – Resolution begins
Each panel is stored separately so the user can edit it.
